00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.406
Paula, what do you think

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.510
An extraordinary moment, Anderson.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.113
The former president was asked to stand

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.215
and enter his own plea

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.016
to the charges

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.450
have been filed against him.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.218
And I'm told he didn't

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.319
even use the microphone.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.920
He just looked straight at the judge

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.589
and projected his voice

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.692
and entered a plea of not guilty.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.092
Now, again,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.427
at the hearing down in Florida,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:28.028
when he went through this

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.462
in a federal courtroom down there,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.663
he had his lawyer enter that.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.698
Pleased to hear him

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.868
say that in his own voice is significant.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.236
Now, the judge is reading

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.405
the conditions of his release.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.240
You may remember that down in Florida,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.007
this is actually what

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.542
delayed the hearing.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:42.976
But here is

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.978
he saying that you must not violate state

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.679
or federal law.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.214
And also that he cannot communicate

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.350
with anyone known to be a witness

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.252
about the case unless through a lawyer.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.087
Now, that could get tricky

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.588
because as we know, he's listening

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.390
